Source landscape: The documentary universe is broad and unusually rich. It spans Turkish administrative and audit records, national statistics, international monitoring, earthquake-response assessments, refugee and social-protection documentation, education and health-system reviews, rights reporting, academic work, and local-language materials. The strongest source families concern social-protection expenditure, poverty and living conditions, health coverage, education access, vulnerable groups, refugee services, earthquake response, reconstruction, and political allocation or exclusion. Search saturation has not been reached.

